IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ddt-dates`
IMPORT `ddt-claims`

-- Dust Diseases Tribunal Act 1989 (NSW) -- cases for every exported question in ddt-claims.l4. Every expected value was
-- worked by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the encoding's output. Days are counted as serial
-- differences: 2 to 23 November 2026 is 21 days, 2 to 30 November 28 days, 2 November to 1 December 29 days.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website, via the Open Australian Legal Corpus
-- (version as at 15 November 2024). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases`

§§ `s 3, Sch 1 -- dust-related condition`

#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `mesothelioma` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `aluminosis` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `silicosis` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `systemic sclerosis` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `talcosis` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum attributable to dust` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `a condition of some other part of the body attributable to dust` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust-related condition` `a condition not attributable to dust` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 10(1), 11 -- the Tribunal's exclusive jurisdiction`

-- Arguments: condition; suffering; breach alleged; who; entitled but for this Act.
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE `the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `asbestosis` TRUE TRUE `their executor, administrator or other legal personal representative` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE `a relative for whose benefit a Compensation to Relatives Act 1897 action may be brought` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `silicosis` TRUE TRUE `another person claiming through the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum attributable to dust` TRUE TRUE `the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE `someone with no claim through the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `a condition not attributable to dust` TRUE TRUE `the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `a condition of some other part of the body attributable to dust` TRUE TRUE `the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `mesothelioma` FALSE TRUE `the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `mesothelioma` TRUE FALSE `the person with the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my claim be brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal` `mesothelioma` TRUE TRUE `the person with the condition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Can I include this other claim in my Tribunal proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I include this other claim in my Tribunal proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I include this other claim in my Tribunal proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I include this other claim in my Tribunal proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Whose leave do I need to sue the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the Tribunal's leave, not the leave of the Court supervising the administration`
#ASSERT `Whose leave do I need to sue the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Whose leave do I need to sue the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

