§§ `s 12 -- transfer`

#ASSERT `Must my case be transferred to the Tribunal` TRUE `the Supreme Court` `brought after section 12 commenced` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my case be transferred to the Tribunal` TRUE `the District Court` `brought after section 12 commenced` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my case be transferred to the Tribunal` TRUE `the Supreme Court` `pending when section 12 commenced, its hearing not yet begun` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my case be transferred to the Tribunal` TRUE `the District Court` `pending when section 12 commenced, its hearing already begun` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must my case be transferred to the Tribunal` TRUE `some other court or tribunal` `brought after section 12 commenced` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must my case be transferred to the Tribunal` FALSE `the Supreme Court` `brought after section 12 commenced` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 12A -- no limitation period`

-- Any claim in the Tribunal, however long after exposure (no date is asked: none could change the answer).
#ASSERT `Can a limitation period stop my Tribunal claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Already determined before s 12A commenced (Sch 3 cl 7(2)): s 12A does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Can a limitation period stop my Tribunal claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not Tribunal proceedings about a dust-related condition.
#ASSERT `Can a limitation period stop my Tribunal claim` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

