§§ `ss 13(5), 32 -- appeal`

#ASSERT `Can I appeal and do I need leave` `a point of law` `a final decision` 20000 EQUALS `I may appeal to the Supreme Court as of right`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and do I need leave` `a point of law` `a final decision` 19999 EQUALS `I may appeal to the Supreme Court only with its leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and do I need leave` `the admission or rejection of evidence` `a final decision` 750000 EQUALS `I may appeal to the Supreme Court as of right`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and do I need leave` `a point of law` `an interlocutory decision` 750000 EQUALS `I may appeal to the Supreme Court only with its leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and do I need leave` `a point of law` `a decision as to costs only` 750000 EQUALS `I may appeal to the Supreme Court only with its leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and do I need leave` `a point of law` `a decision made with the consent of the parties` 750000 EQUALS `I may appeal to the Supreme Court only with its leave`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal and do I need leave` `a question of fact only` `a final decision` 750000 EQUALS `no appeal: section 13(5) leaves only section 48 of the Supreme Court Act 1970`

§§ `s 32I -- claim information`

#ASSERT `Who must give the Registrar my claim information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my solicitor, not my barrister`
#ASSERT `Who must give the Registrar my claim information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my Australian legal practitioner`
#ASSERT `Who must give the Registrar my claim information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I must, because no Australian legal practitioner represents me`

-- Arguments: represented; condition; settled or determined; day; costs to be agreed or assessed; costs done; day;
-- weekday holidays; given; day given; today. Settled Monday 2 November 2026 (8 November 2026 is a Sunday), no costs
-- condition: finalised that day (cl 97(4)(a)). 30 business days counted from Tuesday 3 November: 4 that week, then 5 a
-- week to Friday 11 December (29), so the 30th is Monday 14 December 2026. One weekday holiday moves it to Tuesday 15.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` TRUE `mesothelioma` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `section 32I(4) puts no duty on me, because a legal practitioner represents me`
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `mesothelioma` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 16 11 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `I gave the information within the time`
-- The 30th business day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `mesothelioma` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 14 12 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `I gave the information within the time`
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `mesothelioma` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 15 12 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `I have not given the information within the time: an offence, maximum penalty 5 penalty units`
-- One weekday holiday in the period: 15 December is in time.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `asbestosis` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 1 TRUE (`the date` 15 12 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `I gave the information within the time`
-- Not yet given: on 14 December the time is still running; on 15 December it has ended.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `asbestos related pleural diseases` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 14 12 2026) EQUALS `I have not yet given the information, and the time has not ended`
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `asbestos induced carcinoma` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `I have not given the information within the time: an offence, maximum penalty 5 penalty units`
-- Settled with costs to be assessed; costs assessed Monday 9 November: finalised then (cl 97(4)(b)), so the 30th
-- business day is Monday 21 December. 18 December is in time; costs not yet assessed, the time has not begun.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `asbestosis` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 9 11 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 18 12 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `I gave the information within the time`
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `asbestosis` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the date` 9 11 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 22 12 2026) (`the date` 23 12 2026) EQUALS `I have not given the information within the time: an offence, maximum penalty 5 penalty units`
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `asbestosis` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the time has not begun, because the claim has not been finalised`
-- Not yet settled or determined.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `asbestosis` FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the time has not begun, because the claim has not been finalised`
-- Silicosis and a para (b) condition: cl 97 does not reach them.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `silicosis` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the regulations require no information for this claim: clause 97 reaches only an asbestos-related claim settled or determined on or after 1 July 2005`
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum attributable to dust` TRUE (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the regulations require no information for this claim: clause 97 reaches only an asbestos-related claim settled or determined on or after 1 July 2005`
-- Settled 30 June 2005: before cl 97's day; settled 1 July 2005 and given the same day: in time.
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `mesothelioma` TRUE (`the date` 30 6 2005) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the regulations require no information for this claim: clause 97 reaches only an asbestos-related claim settled or determined on or after 1 July 2005`
#ASSERT `Have I given the claim information in time` FALSE `mesothelioma` TRUE (`the date` 1 7 2005) FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2026) 0 TRUE (`the date` 1 7 2005) (`the date` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `I gave the information within the time`

#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` FALSE `with the consent of the person who provided it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` FALSE `in connection with the administration or execution of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` FALSE `a requirement of a NSW law, other than a subpoena or other compulsory process` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` FALSE `a requirement of a Commonwealth law, other than a subpoena or other compulsory process` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` FALSE `a NSW subpoena or other compulsory process` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Fork F13: the parenthesis qualifies only "a law of the State".
#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` FALSE `a subpoena or other compulsory process under a Commonwealth law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` FALSE `some other reason` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my claim information be recorded or divulged` TRUE `some other reason` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 6 -- interim payments`

-- Arguments: inter-insurer dispute; s 151AB employer; admitted; judgment; substantial damages.
#ASSERT `Can I get interim payments` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Tribunal may order a designated insurer to make interim payments to me under section 43`
#ASSERT `Can I get interim payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Tribunal may order a designated insurer to make interim payments to me under section 43`
#ASSERT `Can I get interim payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the Tribunal may order a designated insurer to make interim payments to me under section 43`
#ASSERT `Can I get interim payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `section 43 applies, but none of its conditions for an order is met`
#ASSERT `Can I get interim payments` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Division 5 of Part 6 of the Civil Procedure Act 2005 extends to my claim under section 41`
#ASSERT `Can I get interim payments` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: inter-insurer dispute unresolved; assessed; assessed amount; likely damages; proportion.
#ASSERT `What is the most the interim payments can be` TRUE TRUE 350000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 350000
#ASSERT `What is the most the interim payments can be` TRUE FALSE 0 400000 0.5 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT `What is the most the interim payments can be` TRUE FALSE 0 400000 0.75 EQUALS JUST 300000
#ASSERT `What is the most the interim payments can be` TRUE FALSE 0 400000 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- No unresolved inter-insurer dispute: s 43 does not apply.
#ASSERT `What is the most the interim payments can be` FALSE TRUE 350000 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Is the interim payment an admission of liability` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the interim payment an admission of liability` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to repay an interim payment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to repay an interim payment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Could I be ordered to repay an interim payment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
